[list]
[*]Fixed: a stand ticked for "Resting in bed" never dressed anybody. Both patient rows in the work list have done nothing since sleepwear arrived in v1.3.0, so a hospital stand set up exactly the way the description says was inert, with nothing on screen to say so. Reported by a player who had read the notes and configured it correctly.
[*]Medical bed rest is a work type like any other again. Put a stand in the hospital, tick "Resting in bed", stock it with gowns, and a colonist going to bed to recuperate changes there on the way. Sleeping is still the separate row for pyjamas, and neither row takes the other's jobs.
[*]A colonist who still needs a doctor goes straight to bed. The gown is for recuperating, so bleeding, waiting on surgery or in labour means no wardrobe stop on the way: someone wounded in a raid reaches the bed first and changes on their next trip, once a doctor has seen them. Nobody is pulled out of a sickbed to change, either.
[*]New setting, "Medical emergencies change first", off by default. Turn it on and the rule above goes away for medical work: a doctor answering an emergency tend puts scrubs on first, and a colonist in critical condition stops for the gown. Fires are never covered by it, whatever it is set to. It applies in both directions, so a doctor already in another room's uniform may change out of that before answering as well.
[*]Both work the same with FrozenSnowFox's Complex Jobs installed. That mod moves a lot of vanilla work onto its own finer-grained job types, which is why a hospital stand there arms for Nurse and Surgeon as well as Doctor, but it leaves bed rest alone and leaves emergency tending under Doctor. Nothing to configure differently either way.
[/list]
